{
  "title": "Sinding-Larsen-Johansson Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3030/sinding-larsen-johansson-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 31 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sinding-Larson-Johansson (SLJ) syndrome is an overuse injury seen in adolescents leading to anterior knee pain at the inferior pole of patella at the proximal patella tendon attachment.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness over the inferior pole of the patella and radiographs of the knee may show a spur at the inferior pole of the patella.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative with NSAIDs, activity modifications and physical therapy with most cases resolving over time.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in adolescence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patellar tendon insertion at the inferior pole of the patella",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "chronic injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "similar pathogenesis to Osgood-Schlatter",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "similar to Osgood-Schlatter disease which is at the distal attachment of the patella tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "overuse causes a traction apophysitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
